    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • Chinese Brand AITO Plans 2027 European Launch\nOver the Hills and Far Away: 1984 Toyota Land Cruiser J60 Has Big Miles But Also Sensible Pricing\n11 photos\nPhoto: Garage Kept Motors / Instagram\nSitting proudly in the inventory of Grand Rapids, Michigan-based Garage Kept Motors , this Copper Metallic and Beige/Tan 4WD Land Cruiser is ready to roll another 100k miles without breaking a sweat – or so we heard.\nThe Toyota Land Cruiser nameplate, alongside the Jeep Wrangler, Land Rover Defender, the Mercedes-Benz G-Class, and just a handful of others, is one of those models that are basically legendary no matter the angle you look at them or the generation you’re assessing. Born in 1951, the model has been in continuous production for no less than three-quarters of a century\nAs such, it has gained a proper cult following, and everyone has their favorites . If you’re an enthusiast of the J60 generation (the Station Wagon series) from the 1980s and early 1990s, then here’s a cool find for you. This is a 1984 Toyota Land Cruiser J60 packing a carbureted 2F straight six which “has that classic Toyota sewing machine sound,” dressed in brown and tan (actually Copper Metallic and beige) with a little over 101k miles on the odometer.\nWhile other vehicles would be at the end of their life cycle at that point, the legendary resilience of the Toyota Land Cruiser promises that, with proper care and maintenance, this SUV is potentially ready for the next 100k miles of adventures and iconic memories. “A classic example of Toyota’s legendary four-wheel-drive utility, combining rugged capability with the practicality and comfort of a traditional SUV,” the FJ60 was purchased new in Texas and spent a decade in the Pacific Northwest and California.\n“Benefitting from life in regions where vintage Land Cruisers remain particularly well appreciated,” the Copper Metallic over Tan SUV has an “unmistakable period-correct appearance that suits the character of this iconic 4x4,” and power comes from under the hood via a “proven” 4.2-liter inline-six-cylinder engine, paired with a 4-speed manual transmission.\nThere’s also four-wheel drive and a robust chassis, so this “Land Cruiser remains just as at home exploring a trail as it is cruising around town.” Most importantly, it has been “maintained with an extensive service history, providing documentation of its care over the years,” and there was an oil change over the summer and also a clean CarFax, it’s ready for “, and anyone looking for a vintage SUV with genuine utility.”\nThe pricing is quite sensible, too, as the dealership wants $36,900 to part ways with it. Meanwhile, a modern round-headlight 2027 Toyota Land Cruiser 1958 comes with a starting price of $58,180 sans destination and potential dealer hikes, and also a modern 326-hp i-Force Max hybrid powertrain featuring a 2.4-liter four-cylinder turbo engine and electric assistance.\nView this post on Instagram A post shared by Garage Kept Motors LLC (@garagekeptmotors)\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n1984 Toyota Land Cruiser J60 toyota land cruiser Toyota Land Cruiser Classic SUV for sale pricing Garage Kept Motors\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT USC Football Star Takes His Dodge Charger Hellcat to a Tuner, Drives Back in a Different Car",
